# Project Conventions - Customer Feedback Module

## Context
Customer-facing feedback form for a gas utility's facilitation center. Customers scan a static QR/barcode at the counter using their own phone and mobile data. On submission, feedback is emailed directly to the incharge. No internet is required anywhere at the office.

## Stack
- Next.js (App Router) + React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
- Server Components by default. Client Components ("use client") only where interactivity is needed, such as the feedback form.
- Server logic lives in route handlers under src/app/api, plus an email service integration
- Design tokens live in src/app/globals.css (@theme block)
- Deployed on Vercel. Every push gets a preview deployment.
- No LAN server, no local database. The Vercel filesystem is read-only, so nothing may be written to disk at runtime.

## Conventions
- Components: PascalCase, one per file, in /src/components
- Types: explicit TypeScript interfaces for feedback data
- Folders: /src/app (routes and route handlers), /src/components, /src/lib, /src/types
- Tests: Vitest, next to the code as *.test.ts. Next.js type-checks them during the build.

## Commit Convention
Conventional Commits: feat, fix, docs, chore, refactor, style, test

## AI Assistant Notes
- Mobile-first, customer's own phone only
- Never assume office/staff internet access
- Trigger email to incharge on submission, no dashboard needed for MVP
- Follow Conventional Commits for commit messages
- Read the bundled Next.js docs in node_modules/next/dist/docs before using an API you are unsure of. This version differs from older ones.

## Rules learned in FE-03
- Phone numbers: strip to digits, require 10-13 digits, reject repeated-digit numbers. Enforce with one shared function in src/lib/validateFeedback.ts, used by the form and by the route handler in src/app/api. Tests must include "0000000000" and "----------".
- Every new function or component ships with a Vitest test in the same commit. Run npm test before committing and report the pass count.
- UI text and source files are ASCII-only. This command must print nothing: git grep -nP "[^\x00-\x7F]" -- src .cursor
- The incharge address exists only in server env config (INCHARGE_EMAIL), never in the repo and never with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Only the variable name may appear, and only in server code (src/lib, src/app/api). These commands must print nothing: git grep -n -E "incharge@" -- src and git grep -n "INCHARGE_EMAIL" -- src/components
- Form controls use <label htmlFor> and aria-describedby for errors. Tests locate fields with getByLabelText or getByRole. Rating buttons show visible text labels ("Very poor" to "Excellent"), not only digits.
- README Status describes the product only. Never write round, week or assignment labels into docs.
